# Kani runs each wrapper on a real atomic, one thread (src/kani/atomic.rs).
# loom and C11 (verus/WEAKMEM.md): arena.rs writes a table entry only
# through `store` (and `Arenas::put_entry`'s write of the atomic `new` made),
# no other file calls these wrappers, and this file mints one EntryPerm
# per atomic, in `new` (tests/loom/tests/access.rs). C++20's coherence
# rules ([intro.races]) give a load the permission's value at its place in
# the entry's modification order; the stores are made under the creation
# lock, which orders them; the `Release` store and an `Acquire` load that
# reads it publish the arena `build` wrote (a release/acquire pair,
# [atomics.order] p2). The narenas model checks that on copies of the
# `Arenas` steps (tests/loom/tests/pins.rs).
store	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::entry_store, and loom: narenas::loom_narenas_create_publishes; not checked: this body under concurrency, which the model replaces with loom's `store` inside copies of the `Arenas` steps, in the configuration tests/loom/src/narenas.rs states; the pointers' provenance (the harness compares addresses); `T = Arena`, the instance challoc uses (checked at `T = u64`); the C11 argument above that the permission's value is the entry's last write, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)
load	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::entry_load, and loom: narenas::loom_narenas_create_publishes; not checked: this body under concurrency, which the model replaces with loom's `load` inside copies of the `Arenas` steps, in the configuration tests/loom/src/narenas.rs states; the pointers' provenance (the harness compares addresses); `T = Arena`, the instance challoc uses (checked at `T = u64`); the C11 argument above, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)
